        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Point Anne, Bay of Quinte, Belleville, Ontario, Canada\n- People: Bobby Hull, Dennis Hull, Manley MacDonald\n- Topics: ghost towns, ice hockey, painting, nicknames\n\nFacts:\n- Point Anne is a ghost town on the Bay of Quinte near Belleville in Ontario, Canada.\n- Point Anne was the birthplace of Bobby Hull, Dennis Hull, and painter Manley MacDonald.\n- Bobby Hull earned the nickname \"The Golden Jet\" for his blonde hair, end-to-end rushes, skating speed, and very high-velocity shot.",
